  "metric_definitions": {
    "ndcg@10": "Graded nDCG over the top 10: gain 2^grade - 1, discount log2(rank + 1), ideal ranking from the query's judged grades. Unjudged passages earn gain 0.",
    "mrr@10": "1 / rank of the first passage judged relevant (grade >= 1) in the top 10, else 0. Unjudged passages count as not relevant.",
    "recall@100": "Judged-relevant passages (grade >= 1) in the top 100 / all judged-relevant passages of the query. The denominator counts known positives only: recall against the pooled judgments, not the corpus.",
    "judged@10": "Share of the top 10 that carries a judgment of any grade (0, 1 or 2).",
    "ndcg@10_judged_only": "nDCG@10 after removing unjudged passages from the ranking (condensed list). Sensitivity check: the score if every unjudged passage were set aside instead of counted as non-relevant.",
    "mrr@10_judged_only": "MRR@10 on the same condensed ranking."
  },
  "unjudged_assumption": "Qrels hold judged passages only (grades 0, 1, 2). An unjudged passage is not a confirmed negative: the standard metrics count it as non-relevant (an assumption), so each query reports how much of its top 10 is judged, how much is a confirmed negative, and how much is unjudged, split into passages from the companies the question asks about (in scope) and from other companies (out of scope).",
